# SELF-RADIATION: bar_self_radiation on adds each band mode's own radiated power per unit modal velocity, W from the receiver's Burton-Miller solve, as max(W, 0) to the loss row's damping; the loss row is the near-vacuum one, so the air counts once. The same term as the C4 tube page, whose tube coupling the engine refused without it.
bar_self_radiation	on
mallet_contact_pack	contact-rubber-mallet-on-padouk-bar-chaigne-doutaut1997
mallet_contact	data/matdb/seed-v1/contact-rubber-mallet-on-padouk-bar-chaigne-doutaut1997/contact.tsv
mallet_properties	data/matdb/seed-v1/mallet-rubber-padouk-bar-chaigne-doutaut1997/properties.tsv
mallet_speed_m_s	1.0
duration_s	4.0
substeps	32
rate_hz	48000
full_scale_pa	2.0
# MODE CERTIFICATE: maximum_relative_halfwidth 1e-6. At the earlier card's 1e-7 the seventh scan of the engine cut solve (reach 74.794 mm, middle 5.491 mm), after six scans that certified at 1e-7, was refused in window 1 at all four window counts, on the mode at 331.126 Hz, f1 on that cut: relative half-widths 8.78e-7, 3.58e-6, 2.17e-7 and 1.25e-6 at 10, 11, 12 and 13 windows (FS-MODAL-HALFWIDTH-EXCEEDED), the worst 3.58e-6. A relative half-width is the eigenvalue's, so at f1 the worst is 5.9e-4 Hz, 0.0031 c, and the 1e-6 row bounds it at 1.7e-4 Hz, 0.00087 c: a certificate tolerance more than two orders of magnitude below audibility. It sets no sound. 1e-6 is the next decade, as on the C4 card.
maximum_relative_halfwidth	1e-6
tube	closed_open
tube_radius_m	0.0265
tube_air_length_m	0.241000
tube_gap_m	0.0127
tube_modes	4
# RECEIVER: the broadband observer (e6313e19d): one delay and an order-16 rational fit of the boundary-element transfer from each bar mode to the receiver, checked on held-out frequencies against a 5 % budget. It hears the bar during the mallet's contact and with its travel time; the narrow-band law it replaces passed the contact force as a pulse.
observer	broadband
observer_fit_order	16
observer_held_out_budget	0.05
observer_rigid_rows	on
